212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 59 0 R
/T (E-commerce platforms are widely used for online shopping, product searching, and sales management. As the number of products and users increases, maintaining fast and efficient system performance becomes important. ShopSphere is an online shopping platform that currently manages 100,000 products and is expected to reach 1,000,000 products within a year. This growth may increase processing time and affect system performance. This assessment analyses five backend modules: Duplicate-Listing Detector, API Rate Limiter, Product Search, Recommendation Engine, and Sales Analytics Engine. Using algorithm analysis techniques such as Big-O notation, Big-Theta notation, Master Theorem, and substitution method, the efficiency of each module is evaluated. The main aim is to identify performance problems and recommend suitable algorithm improvements to make ShopSphere scalable and efficient. )
/E (E-commerce platforms are widely used for online shopping, product searching, and sales management. As the number of products and users increases, maintaining fast and efficient system performance becomes important. ShopSphere is an online shopping platform that currently manages 100,000 products and is expected to reach 1,000,000 products within a year. This growth may increase processing time and affect system performance. This assessment analyses five backend modules: Duplicate-Listing Detector, API Rate Limiter, Product Search, Recommendation Engine, and Sales Analytics Engine. Using algorithm analysis techniques such as Big-O notation, Big-Theta notation, Master Theorem, and substitution method, the efficiency of each module is evaluated. The main aim is to identify performance problems and recommend suitable algorithm improvements to make ShopSphere scalable and efficient. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
